<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pompey</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pompey was a Roman general and statesman of the first century BCE. During his eastern campaigns he annexed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> in 63 BCE. This ended the remnant of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a> and made Syria a Roman province.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pompey.jpg" alt="Pompey" width="277" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Didier Descouens · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:(Venice)_Pompey_the_Great,_Museo_Archeologico_Nazionale.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
